# debugger_dialogue.script with typing mistakes taken back by Backspace
# and Delete (standard_io_window getl/2's rubout, window M11, OURS): the
# dots must come out as the dialogue's (test_boot_route.SCREEN_SHA).
#  - the first goal wraps after `Re` (44 columns): four Backspaces rub out
#    `q).` and, from column 0, the `e` at the end of the row above, which
#    is typed again;
#  - `pimos` typed as `pimps`, Delete twice;
#  - the password (echo off) gets a wrong letter taken back unseen.
click r 640 560
click r 640 560
click l 700 589
quiet
type :create(#pimfep##pimos_login_requester,Req).
key bs
key bs
key bs
key bs
type eq).
key enter
quiet
type :create(#process,Prox
key bs
type c).
key enter
quiet
type :activate(Proc,Req).
key enter
quiet
type local
key enter
quiet
type pimps
key del
key del
type os
key enter
quiet
type secrex
key bs
type t
key enter
quiet
